<%# One day or a week of entries on the time grid, drawing the hours of the user's slice (hours=); more_href leads to where a day's overflow can be read; path is the page's own path helper; scroll says whether the page scrolls by itself to the current time when it opens %>
<%= render Core::UI::TimeGridComponent.new(
      days: ((period.view == :week) ? period.days_of_week : [period.date]).map { |date| {date:, entries: entries_by_day.fetch(date, [])} }, today: Date.current,
      agenda_href: more_href, now: Time.current, scroll:, **time_grid_options(period, path:)
    ) %>
